
Below is a complete step-by-step flow of one BERT-Base encoder block with all operations included:

Multi-Head Attention
Residual connection
Dropout
LayerNorm
Feed Forward Network
Residual again
Dropout again
LayerNorm again

Using BERT-Base dimensions.

Model: BERT

1️⃣ BERT-Base Configuration
Parameter	            Value
Layers	            12 encoder blocks
Hidden size	            768
Attention heads	      12
Head dimension	      64
Feedforward dimension	3072
Max tokens	            512

Head dimension:

768/12=64
768/12=64
2️⃣ Example Input Sentence

Sentence:

"I love transformers"

After tokenization:

[CLS] I love transformers [SEP]

Total tokens:

5 tokens
3️⃣ Embedding Layer

Each token becomes 768-dim vector

Embeddings added together:

Token Embedding
+ Position Embedding
+ Segment Embedding

Result tensor:

X shape = (5 , 768)

Example simplified vector for one token:

[CLS] = [0.2, 0.1, -0.4 ... 768]
4️⃣ Start Encoder Block

Input to encoder block:

X = (5 × 768)
5️⃣ Multi-Head Self Attention

First compute Q, K, V

Q = XWq
K = XWk
V = XWv

Weights:

Wq = (768 × 768)
Wk = (768 × 768)
Wv = (768 × 768)

Output shapes:

Q = (5 × 768)
K = (5 × 768)
V = (5 × 768)
6️⃣ Split into 12 Heads

Each head dimension:

64

Reshape:

Q → (5 , 12 , 64)
K → (5 , 12 , 64)
V → (5 , 12 , 64)
7️⃣ Attention Score

For each head compute:

QKᵀ

Dimension:

(5 × 64) × (64 × 5) = (5 × 5)

Scale by √dk.

dk = 64
8️⃣ Attention Softmax

Softmax over tokens:

Example attention matrix:

5 × 5

Example row:

[0.1 0.3 0.4 0.1 0.1]

Meaning token attends to other tokens.

9️⃣ Multiply With V
Attention × V

Shape:

(5 × 5) × (5 × 64)

Result:

(5 × 64)

Each head output.

🔟 Concatenate Heads

12 heads:

12 × 64 = 768

Result:

(5 × 768)
1️⃣1️⃣ Final Attention Projection

Multiply with output matrix:

Wo = (768 × 768)

Output:

Attention_output = (5 × 768)
1️⃣2️⃣ Dropout

BERT applies dropout (usually 0.1).

Attention_output = Dropout(Attention_output)

Shape unchanged:

(5 × 768)
1️⃣3️⃣ Residual Connection

Add original input:

Z1 = X + Attention_output

Shape:

(5 × 768)

Residual helps gradient flow.

1️⃣4️⃣ Layer Normalization

Normalize each token vector.

LayerNorm formula:

LN(x) = (x − mean) / sqrt(var + ε) * γ + β

Output:

Z1_norm = LayerNorm(Z1)

Shape:

(5 × 768)
1️⃣5️⃣ Feed Forward Network

First linear layer:

W1 = (768 × 3072)

Multiply:

(5 × 768) × (768 × 3072)

Result:

(5 × 3072)
1️⃣6️⃣ Activation Function

BERT uses GELU.

FF1 = GELU(Z1_norm W1 + b1)

Shape:

(5 × 3072)
1️⃣7️⃣ Second Linear Layer
W2 = (3072 × 768)

Multiply:

(5 × 3072) × (3072 × 768)

Result:

(5 × 768)
1️⃣8️⃣ Dropout Again
FF2 = Dropout(FF2)

Shape:

(5 × 768)
1️⃣9️⃣ Residual Connection Again

Add skip connection:

Z2 = Z1_norm + FF2

Shape:

(5 × 768)
2️⃣0️⃣ LayerNorm Again
Output = LayerNorm(Z2)

Final output:

(5 × 768)

This becomes input to next encoder block.

2️⃣1️⃣ Full Encoder Block Summary
Input (5×768)
      ↓
